  "plan": "## Feature Implementation Plan: Add code path to board\n\n### Overview\nAdd `code_path` field to project config and support for `CONTEXT.md` file so AI agents know the project root location and have access to project-level context. Agents should start from project root, not work item directory.\n\n### 1. Config Schema Changes\n\n#### File Location\n- Config file: `<project_root>/.mad.config.json` (per-project, not global)\n- Context file: `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md` (optional, missing is OK)\n\n#### Config Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"code_path\": \"/absolute/path/to/project/root\",\n  \"context_file\": \".mad/CONTEXT.md\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Field Definitions\n- `code_path`: Absolute path to project root. If not set, use default derivation.\n- `context_file`: Relative path from project root to context file (default: `.mad/CONTEXT.md`)\n\n### 2. code_path Derivation Logic\n\n#### Default Derivation Algorithm\nWhen `code_path` is not explicitly set in config:\n1. Start with board location: `~/.mad/boards/<boardname>/`\n2. Go up two levels: `board_dir.parent.parent` → project root\n3. Example: `~/.mad/boards/myboard/ideas/abc123/` → project root is parent of `boards`\n4. Resolve symlinks at read time using `os.path.realpath()` (handles symlink chains)\n5. If path doesn't exist (new project), allow it without validation failure\n\n#### Per-Board Override\nEach project can have its own `<project_root>/.mad.config.json` with `code_path` set explicitly. Per-board config takes precedence - no merge with defaults.\n\n### 3. CONTEXT.md Handling\n\n#### File Location\n- Default: `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n- Configurable via `context_file` field in config\n\n#### Reading and Size Handling\n1. Attempt to read context file when agent is invoked\n2. If file missing or permission denied: silently ignore, proceed without context\n3. If file exists and readable:\n   - Read content\n   - If content > 100KB: truncate at UTF-8 character boundary nearest to 100KB\n   - Use encoding-aware truncation to avoid corrupting multi-byte characters\n\n#### CLI Commands (Required Implementation)\n- `mad context edit`: Open CONTEXT.md in editor, create if doesn't exist\n- `mad context view`: Display current CONTEXT.md content\n- `mad config set code_path <path>`: Set project root path in config\n- `mad config show`: Display current config including code_path\n\n### 4. Agent Invocation Changes\n\n#### Working Directory\n- When invoking an agent, set working directory to `code_path` (project root), not the work item directory\n- Use `os.chdir(code_path)` or pass `cwd` parameter to agent execution\n\n#### Instruction Prepending (Per Session, Not Per Message)\nFor each new agent session, prepend to initial instructions:\n```\nProject Root: <code_path>\nContext File: <project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md\n\n[CONTENT OF CONTEXT.MD IF EXISTS]\n\n---\n```\n\n- Only prepend once at session start, not every message\n- If CONTEXT.md doesn't exist, still include the path in instructions\n- Include actual context content if file is readable\n\n### 5. Implementation Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Config Module Updates\n- Add `code_path` and `context_file` fields to config schema\n- Implement `get_code_path(board_name)` function with derivation logic\n- Implement `resolve_symlinks(path)` using `os.path.realpath()`\n- Add config validation for path format (must be absolute)\n\n#### Step 2: Context File Module\n- Implement `read_context_file(project_root, context_file_path)` function\n- Add size check (100KB limit) with UTF-8 safe truncation:\n  ```python\n  def truncate_at_boundary(content, max_bytes=100*1024):\n      if len(content.encode('utf-8')) <= max_bytes:\n          return content\n      truncated = content.encode('utf-8')[:max_bytes]\n      return truncated.decode('utf-8', errors='ignore')\n  ```\n- Handle missing file gracefully (return empty string)\n\n#### Step 3: Agent Invocation Updates\n- Modify agent launcher to:\n  1. Read config for `code_path`\n  2. Set working directory to `code_path`\n  3. Read CONTEXT.md content\n  4. Prepend context to initial agent prompt\n\n#### Step 4: CLI Commands\n- Implement `mad context edit` using editor (fallback to $EDITOR or vim)\n- Implement `mad context view` to display content\n- Implement `mad config set code_path <path>` to write config\n- Implement `mad config show` to display all config\n\n### 6. Security Considerations\n\n#### Path Validation (Future Enhancement)\n- Document that malicious code in project root could be executed by agent\n- Create tracking item for future security hardening:\n  - Block sensitive paths: /etc, /var, /usr, /root, ~/.ssh, ~/.aws, etc.\n  - Path traversal prevention\n  - Escape to parent directory detection\n\n### 7. Error Handling\n\n| Scenario | Behavior |\n|----------|----------|\n| Config file missing | Use default derivation |\n| code_path not in config | Derive from board location |\n| CONTEXT.md missing | Include path in instructions, proceed without content |\n| CONTEXT.md > 100KB | Truncate at UTF-8 character boundary |\n| CONTEXT.md permission denied | Silently ignore, proceed without content |\n| Symlink in code_path | Resolve to real path at read time |\n| code_path doesn't exist | Allow (for new projects) |\n\n### 8. Backward Compatibility\n- No config version handling needed (new fields are additive)\n- Existing configs without code_path continue to work with derivation\n- No migration required"
